[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Color Modes and Dark Mode Implementation in Bootstrap"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"Bootstrap 5.3 introduced native support for color modes, most notably dark mode. Instead of relying on custom stylesheets or complex class toggles, Bootstrap now utilizes the 'data-bs-theme' HTML attribute. This allows developers to easily switch the entire page, or specific components, between light and dark themes dynamically."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"Enabling Dark Mode Globally"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"To apply dark mode globally across your entire application, add the 'data-bs-theme="dark"' attribute to the root '<html>' element. This automatically updates all Bootstrap components, utility classes, and CSS variables to their dark variants."},{"order":5,"type":"code","text":"<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en" data-bs-theme="dark">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <link href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap@5.3.0/dist/css/bootstrap.min.css" rel="stylesheet">
    <title>Bootstrap Dark Mode</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <div class="container my-5">
      <h1>Hello, Dark Mode!</h1>
      <p class="text-muted">This page is rendered using Bootstrap's native dark theme.</p>
      <button class="btn btn-primary">Primary Button</button>
    </div>
  </body>
</html>"},{"order":6,"type":"subheading","text":"Component-Level Color Modes"},{"order":7,"type":"paragraph","text":"You can also apply color modes to specific components or containers rather than the entire document. For example, you can have a dark navbar on an otherwise light page by adding 'data-bs-theme="dark"' directly to the '<nav>' element."},{"order":8,"type":"code","text":"<nav class="navbar navbar-expand-lg bg-body-tertiary" data-bs-theme="dark">
  <div class="container-fluid">
    <a class="navbar-brand" href="#">Navbar</a>
    <button class="navbar-toggler" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#navbarNav">
      <span class="navbar-toggler-icon"></span>
    </button>
  </div>
</nav>"},{"order":9,"type":"subheading","text":"Building a Dynamic Theme Switcher"},{"order":10,"type":"paragraph","text":"To allow users to toggle between light, dark, and system-default modes, you can use a simple JavaScript script. This script listens for changes, updates the 'data-bs-theme' attribute, and saves the user's preference to local storage."},{"order":11,"type":"code","text":"const getStoredTheme = () => localStorage.getItem('theme');
const setStoredTheme = theme => localStorage.setItem('theme', theme);

const getPreferredTheme = () => {
  const storedTheme = getStoredTheme();
  if (storedTheme) {
    return storedTheme;
  }
  return window.matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: dark)').matches ? 'dark' : 'light';
};

const setTheme = theme => {
  if (theme === 'auto') {
    document.documentElement.setAttribute('data-bs-theme', (window.matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: dark)').matches ? 'dark' : 'light'));
  } else {
    document.documentElement.setAttribute('data-bs-theme', theme);
  }
};

// Apply theme on load
setTheme(getPreferredTheme());"},{"order":12,"type":"subheading","text":"Customizing Themes with Sass"},{"order":13,"type":"paragraph","text":"Bootstrap's color modes are built using CSS variables, making them highly customizable. You can override the default dark mode colors or define entirely new color modes by modifying the Sass maps '$color-modes' in your custom stylesheet."},{"order":14,"type":"code","text":"@import "bootstrap/scss/functions";
@import "bootstrap/scss/variables";
@import "bootstrap/scss/variables-dark";
@import "bootstrap/scss/maps";
@import "bootstrap/scss/mixins";

// Customizing the dark mode background
$color-modes: (
  "light": (),
  "dark": (
    "body-bg": #121212,
    "body-color": #e0e0e0,
    "primary": #0d6efd
  )
);

@import "bootstrap/scss/bootstrap";"},{"order":15,"type":"subheading","text":"Best Practices for Dark Mode"},{"order":16,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Always use Bootstrap's semantic color utility classes (like 'text-body', 'bg-body', and 'border-color') instead of hardcoded hex values to ensure seamless transition between modes."},{"order":17,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Test your custom components in both light and dark modes to verify text contrast ratios meet WCAG accessibility guidelines."},{"order":18,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Leverage the 'prefers-color-scheme' media query to automatically match the user's operating system preference on their first visit."}]
